<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wewoka, Oklahoma</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wewoka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wewoka is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a>, founded in 1849 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-seminoles">Black Seminoles</a> led by John Horse. It became the capital of the Seminole Nation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-territory">Indian Territory</a> and remains the seat of Seminole County. Its name is said to mean barking water in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Muscogee</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wewoka-oklahoma.jpg" alt="Wewoka, Oklahoma" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kennethaw88 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seminole_County_OK_Courthouse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
